title: Public Order Reform
new-page: true
choose-if: party_resources > 0 and not parlament_police_passed
subtitle: [? if coming_from_parlament: \[-1 resources\]?]
unavailable-subtitle: [? if parlament_police_passed: Already approved!?][? if not parlament_police_passed and party_resources < 1: Not enough resources.?]
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament) Q.party_resources -= 1;
!}

= Public Order Reform

After a woman lost her eye in an anti-austerity protest due to police-shot rubber bullets, a broader crisis related to public-police trust has emerged. With Catalonia having its own police force in the form of the Mossos d'Esquadra, it is clear that the Generalitat and the Parlament have a responsibility to fulfill here.

Official recommendations call for a ban on rubber bullets all together and reforming crowd-control protocols to "better balance the right to protest with public order and safety". However, social movements are demanding more in-depth police reforms. These talk about police democratization, independent watchdogs, and structural reforms to the chains of command to root-out impunity.

- @police_focused
- @police_democratic

@police_focused
title: Focus on surgical reforms and banning rubber bullets
choose-if: player_party != "cup"
unavailable-subtitle: Such a soft reform has too many opponents within the party.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_police_variant = "focused_reform";
    var proposingParty = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    Q.parlament_police_yes_names = ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cs","si"];
    Q.parlament_police_no_names = ["ppc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament && !Q.parlament_police_yes_names.includes(proposingParty)) {
        Q.parlament_police_yes_names.push(proposingParty);
    }
    Q.parlament_police_deals = [];
!}
go-to: police_negotiation

Such a surgical change to policing, without any in-depth addressing of the root causes of police violence, hardly convinces those to the left of the political spectrum. We may want to approach them if we want to secure an ample majority for this vote.

@police_democratic
title: Push for the democratization of policing
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_police_variant = "democratic_policing";
    var proposingParty = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    Q.parlament_police_yes_names = ["erc","cup","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","si"];
    Q.parlament_police_no_names = ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","junts","ppc","cs","unio","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament && !Q.parlament_police_yes_names.includes(proposingParty)) {
        Q.parlament_police_yes_names.push(proposingParty);
    }
    Q.parlament_police_deals = [];
!}
go-to: police_negotiation

While it is unsurprising that right-wing parties oppose such a reform to policing, more traditional parties towards the centre of the political spectrum also think of it as a bit of a radical approach. We may want to approach them if we want to secure an ample majority for this vote.

@police_negotiation
on-arrival: {!
    function canApproach(party, eligible) {
        if (!eligible || !party) return false;
        if ((Q[party + "_parlament_s"] || 0) <= 0) return false;
        if (Q.parlament_police_yes_names.includes(party)) return false;
        return !Q.parlament_police_deals.some(function (deal) { return deal.party == party; });
    }

    var ercPlayer = Q.player_party == "erc";
    var cupPlayer = Q.player_party == "cup";
    Q.parlament_police_can_approach_cup = canApproach("cup", ercPlayer);
    Q.parlament_police_can_approach_psc = canApproach("psc", ercPlayer);
    Q.parlament_police_can_approach_erc = canApproach("erc", cupPlayer);
    Q.parlament_police_can_approach_convergence = canApproach(Q.parlament_current_ciu, ercPlayer || cupPlayer);
    Q.parlament_police_can_approach_icv = canApproach(Q.parlament_current_icv, ercPlayer || cupPlayer);
!}


- @police_approach_cup
- @police_approach_psc
- @police_approach_erc
- @police_approach_convergence
- @police_approach_icv
- @police_vote: Proceed with the vote

@police_approach_cup
title: Approach the CUP before the vote
view-if: parlament_police_can_approach_cup
choose-if: cup_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with the CUP
on-arrival: parlament_police_deal_party = "cup"
go-to: police_make_deal

· The CUP will not oppose our proposal.

@police_approach_psc
title: Approach the PSC before the vote
view-if: parlament_police_can_approach_psc
choose-if: psc_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with the PSC
on-arrival: parlament_police_deal_party = "psc"
go-to: police_make_deal

· The PSC will not oppose our proposal.

@police_approach_erc
title: Approach ERC before the vote
view-if: parlament_police_can_approach_erc
choose-if: psc_relations > 55
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with ERC
on-arrival: parlament_police_deal_party = "erc"
go-to: police_make_deal

· ERC will not oppose our proposal.

@police_approach_convergence
title: Approach [+ parlament_current_ciu +] before the vote
choose-if: (ciu_parlament_s > 0 and ciu_relations > 55) or (cdc_parlament_s > 0 and cdc_relations > 55) or (dl_parlament_s > 0 and dl_relations > 0) or (pdcat_parlament_s > 0 and ciu_relations > 55 and not pdcat_split) or (jxcat_parlament_s > 0 and jxcat_relations > 55 and not player_in_jxcat) or (junts_parlament_s > 0 and junts_relations > 55)
view-if: parlament_police_can_approach_convergence
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_ciu +]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_police_deal_party = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
!}
go-to: police_make_deal

· [+ parlament_current_ciu +] will not oppose our proposal.

@police_approach_icv
title: Approach [+ parlament_current_icv +] before the vote
view-if: parlament_police_can_approach_icv
choose-if: (icv_parlament_s > 0 and icv_relations > 55) or (csq_parlament_s > 0 and csqp_relations > 55) or (cecp_parlament_s > 0 and cecp_relations > 55) or (ecp_parlament_s > 0 and ecp_relations > 55)
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_icv +]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_police_deal_party = Q.parlament_current_icv;
!}
go-to: police_make_deal

· [+ parlament_current_icv +] will not oppose our proposal.

@police_make_deal
on-arrival: {!
    var party = Q.parlament_police_deal_party;
    var baselineNo = Q.parlament_police_no_names.includes(party);
    var newPosition = baselineNo && Q[party + "_relations"] <= 65 ? "abstain" : "yes";
    Q.parlament_police_deals.push({party: party, position: newPosition});
    Q[party + "_relations"] -= 5;
!}
go-to: police_negotiation

@police_vote
subtitle: [? if not parlament_police_deal_party: Who needs their support anyway? ?]
on-arrival: {!
    var playerProposal = Q.coming_from_parlament;
    var proposingParty = Q.player_in_jxsi ? "jxsi" : Q.player_in_jxcat ? "jxcat" : Q.player_party;
    Q.coming_from_parlament = false;

    var democratic = Q.parlament_police_variant == "democratic_policing";
    var author = proposingParty;
    var reformDonor = Q.parlament_current_icv;
    if (reformDonor == author || (Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_s"] || 0) <= 0) reformDonor = "psc";
    if (reformDonor == author || (Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_s"] || 0) <= 0) reformDonor = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
    var orderParty = (Q.cs_parlament_s || 0) > 0 && author != "cs" ? "cs" : "ppc";

    var proposalYoung = democratic ? 0.105 : 0.036;
    var proposalMiddle = democratic ? 0 : 0.024;
    var proposalWorker = democratic ? 0.075 : 0;
    var proposalRetiredLoss = democratic ? 0.036 : 0;
    var proposalBusinessLoss = democratic ? 0.03 : 0;
    var proposalRuralLoss = democratic ? 0.024 : 0;
    for (const c of Q.parlament_constituencies) {
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] += proposalYoung;
        Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] -= proposalYoung;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] += proposalMiddle;
        Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] -= proposalMiddle;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_ind_support"] += proposalWorker;
        Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_ind_support"] -= proposalWorker;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_retired_support"] -= proposalRetiredLoss;
        Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_retired_support"] += proposalRetiredLoss;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_buss_support"] -= proposalBusinessLoss;
        Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_buss_support"] += proposalBusinessLoss;
        Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_rural_support"] -= proposalRuralLoss;
        Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_rural_support"] += proposalRuralLoss;
    }

    // TODO: Refine ERC, PSC and JxSi/JxCat positions by leadership after playtesting.
    var yesNames = (Q.parlament_police_yes_names || []).slice();
    var noNames = (Q.parlament_police_no_names || []).slice();
    // Old saves or direct scene jumps may not have passed through the
    // negotiation setup, so retain the authored vote map as a fallback.
    if (yesNames.length == 0 && noNames.length == 0) {
        yesNames = democratic
            ? ["erc","cup","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","si"]
            : ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cs","si"];
        noNames = democratic
            ? ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","junts","ppc","cs","unio","vox","pxc","fnc"]
            : ["ppc","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","vox","pxc","fnc"];
        if (playerProposal && !yesNames.includes(proposingParty)) yesNames.push(proposingParty);
    }
    for (const deal of (Q.parlament_police_deals || [])) {
        yesNames = yesNames.filter(function (party) { return party != deal.party; });
        noNames = noNames.filter(function (party) { return party != deal.party; });
        if (deal.position == "yes") yesNames.push(deal.party);
    }
    var all = ["ciu","cdc","dl","pdcat","jxsi","jxcat","junts","erc","cup","psc","ppc","cs","icv","csqp","cecp","ecp","unio","si","vox","pxc","fnc"];
    var labels = {ciu:"CiU",cdc:"CDC",dl:"DL",pdcat:"PDeCAT",jxsi:"JxSÃ­",jxcat:"JxCat",junts:"Junts",erc:"ERC",cup:"CUP",psc:"PSC",ppc:"PPC",cs:"Cs",icv:"ICV-EUiA",csqp:"CSQP",cecp:"CECP",ecp:"ECP",unio:"UDC",si:"SI",vox:"Vox",pxc:"PxC",fnc:"FNC"};
    var yesParties = [], noParties = [], abstainParties = [];
    Q.parlament_police_yes = 0;
    Q.parlament_police_no = 0;
    Q.parlament_police_abst = 0;
    for (const p of all) {
        var seats = Q[p + "_parlament_s"] || 0;
        if (seats <= 0) continue;
        if (yesNames.includes(p)) {
            Q.parlament_police_yes += seats;
            yesParties.push({label:labels[p]});
        } else if (noNames.includes(p)) {
            Q.parlament_police_no += seats;
            noParties.push({label:labels[p]});
        } else {
            Q.parlament_police_abst += seats;
            abstainParties.push({label:labels[p]});
        }
    }
    Q.parlament_police_passed = Q.parlament_police_yes > Q.parlament_police_no;
    Q.parlament_police_vote_result = {outcomes:[
        {kind:"yes",label:"Yes",votes:Q.parlament_police_yes,parties:yesParties},
        {kind:"abstain",label:"Abstention",votes:Q.parlament_police_abst,parties:abstainParties},
        {kind:"no",label:"No",votes:Q.parlament_police_no,parties:noParties}
    ]};

    if (Q.parlament_police_passed) {
        var passageYoung = democratic ? 0.245 : 0.084;
        var passageMiddle = democratic ? 0 : 0.056;
        var passageWorker = democratic ? 0.175 : 0;
        var passageRetiredLoss = democratic ? 0.084 : 0;
        var passageBusinessLoss = democratic ? 0.07 : 0;
        var passageRuralLoss = democratic ? 0.056 : 0;
        for (const c of Q.parlament_constituencies) {
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] += passageYoung;
            Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_young_support"] -= passageYoung;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] += passageMiddle;
            Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_middle_support"] -= passageMiddle;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_ind_support"] += passageWorker;
            Q[reformDonor + "_parlament_" + c + "_ind_support"] -= passageWorker;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_retired_support"] -= passageRetiredLoss;
            Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_retired_support"] += passageRetiredLoss;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_buss_support"] -= passageBusinessLoss;
            Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_buss_support"] += passageBusinessLoss;
            Q[author + "_parlament_" + c + "_rural_support"] -= passageRuralLoss;
            Q[orderParty + "_parlament_" + c + "_rural_support"] += passageRuralLoss;
        }
        if (democratic) {
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"democratic_policing",title:"Law on Democratic Policing",group:"rights",icon:"img/fist_icon.png",targets:{generalitat_surplus:-0.012,social_dissent_eq:-2.5},ramp_ticks:8});
        } else {
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"public_order_focused_reform",title:"Public Order Reform",group:"rights",icon:"img/fist_icon.png",targets:{social_dissent_eq:-1},ramp_ticks:3});
        }
    }
!}

<div data-widget="chamber-vote" data-props='{"configFrom":"parlament_police_vote_result"}'></div>

[? if parlament_police_passed and parlament_police_variant == "focused_reform": The Parlament has approved the reform. Rubber bullets are now banned, and crowd-control protocols are to be rewritten around mediation and de-escalation.?]
[? if parlament_police_passed and parlament_police_variant == "democratic_policing": The Parlament has approved the Law on Democratic Policing. An independent investigation body will now have to be built in the face of resistance from police unions and parts of the Interior hierarchy.?]
[? if not parlament_police_passed: The Parlament has rejected the reform. Public concern over policing will not change without any further actions, so we may want to re-introduce this proposal at a later date.?]

- @post_event: Continue...
